# Outputing multiple values from Livebook cells

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:obsidian_livebook, github: "scossar/obsidian_livebook"},
  :kino
])
```

## The problem

When a Livebook cell is evaluated, the result of the last evaluation is printed to the Livebook output cell:

```elixir
a = 1 + 1
b = 1 + 2
c = 1 + 3
```

For learning purposes, I often want to be able to see the values produced by multiple expressions.

## Piping into `IO.puts`

This seems to work:

```elixir
a = 1 + 1 |> IO.puts
b = 1 + 2 |> IO.puts
c = 1 + 3 |> IO.puts
```

But it falls apart if something more needs to be done with the assigned values - `IO.puts` returns `:ok` on success

```elixir
a = 1 + 1 |> IO.puts
b = a + 1 |> IO.puts  # `b = :ok + 1
# ** (ArithmeticError) bad argument in arithmetic expression: :ok + 1
```

A possible workaround is to assign the variables first, then pipe them to `IO.puts`

```elixir
a = 1 + 1
a |> IO.puts
b = a + 1
b |> IO.puts
```

## Piping into `IO.inspect`

[`IO.inspect`](https://elixir.hexdocs.pm/IO.html#inspect/2) handles maps, tuples, etc, supports labels, and *returns the original value*. So this will work:

```elixir
a = 1 + 1 |> IO.inspect
b = a + 1 |> IO.inspect
c = a + b |> IO.inspect
```

```elixir
my_range = (1..23) |> IO.inspect(label: "my_range")
```

## Piping into `Kino.inspect`

Import [Kino](https://kino.hexdocs.pm/0.19.1/Kino.html) into the project and use [Kino.Inspect](https://kino.hexdocs.pm/0.19.1/Kino.Inspect.html).

"Kino is a library used by Livebook to render rich and interactive outputs directly from your Elixir code." That seems suitable for the task.

`Kino.inspect` is a "meta-struct that implements the [`Kino.Render`](https://kino.hexdocs.pm/0.19.1/Kino.Render.html) protocol, so that the wrapped value is rendered using the inspect protocol". Which seems to indicate the `Kino.inspect` is a drop-in replacement for `IO.inspect`, but with some additional functionality.

<!-- livebook:{"force_markdown":true} -->

```elixir
Mix.install([
  :kino
])
```

```elixir
my_range = (1..23) |> Kino.inspect(label: "my_range")
a = 1 + 1 |> Kino.inspect(label: "a = 1 + 1")
b = a + 1 |> Kino.inspect(label: "b = a + 1")
c = a + b |> Kino.inspect(label: "c = a + b")
```

## Publish to Obsidian

```elixir
ObsidianLivebook.publish("/home/scossar/obsidian_vault", __ENV__.file)
```
